<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tabaristan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tabaristan was the medieval name of the Caspian province of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, roughly modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran">Mazandaran</a>, a land of forested mountains and coastal lowlands. Shielded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alborz">Alborz</a>, it kept Zoroastrian rulers such as the Dabuyids for over a century after the Arab conquest, and local dynasties including the Bavandids, Qarinvandids and Paduspanids survived for centuries. In 864 it became the base of the Zaydi Alavid state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tabaristan.jpg" alt="Tabaristan" width="320" height="149" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HistoryofIran · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northern_Iran_and_its_surroundings_during_the_Iranian_intermezzo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
